// ndfault.nv — the one thing that can go wrong, and the nine ways it
// does.
//
// One error type covers the whole package.  Every failure here is the
// same failure wearing a different hat.  The caller asked for an
// operation the shapes do not admit: two arrays that cannot be
// broadcast, an axis that is not there, an index off the end, a
// reshape whose element count does not match, a mean of nothing.  A
// second error type would only make a caller decide which `match` to
// write, and the answer would always be "both".
//
// Every variant carries the numbers it compared.  A shape failure is a
// mistake about dimensions, and a message that does not print the
// dimensions sends the reader back to the source to guess which of the
// four arrays in the expression was the wrong one.  `message` prints
// both sides.
//
// Every variant name carries the `Nd` prefix.  An enum variant is
// constructed by its bare name across the whole assembly, so
// `ShapeMismatch` declared here would bind every `ShapeMismatch` in
// any program that also depends on a package that declared one.  The
// prefix is what keeps this package composable, and it is the rule in
// `docs/publishing.md`, "Public type names are globally unique".

// What an array operation could not do, and the shapes that made it
// impossible.
//
// ```novo
// use ndfault
//
// fn main() [io]
//     let e = NdAxisOutOfRange(3, 2)
//     println(e.message())
// ```
pub enum NdFault
    // Two arrays had to agree exactly and did not.  `want` is the
    // shape the operation was already committed to, which is the left
    // operand or the destination.  `got` is the one that did not fit.
    NdShapeMismatch(want: [Int], got: [Int])
    // Two shapes could not be broadcast against each other.  The rule
    // they failed is written once, in `ndshape.broadcast`.  This
    // variant reports only the pair, because a reader who knows the
    // rule needs the pair and a reader who does not needs the page.
    NdNotBroadcastable(left: [Int], right: [Int])
    // An axis number that is not an axis of this array.  Axes are
    // 0-based and count from the outermost, so the legal range is
    // `[0, rank)` and a negative axis is not accepted.  numpy counts a
    // negative axis from the end, which reads badly in a language whose
    // lists do not index that way.
    NdAxisOutOfRange(axis: Int, rank: Int)
    // A full index that is off the array.  Both lists are here because
    // either half can be the mistake.  There may be too few
    // coordinates, or one coordinate may be too large.
    NdIndexOutOfRange(index: [Int], dims: [Int])
    // An index list of the wrong length for the array's rank.  It is
    // separate from `NdIndexOutOfRange` because the fix is different.
    // This one is a coordinate the caller forgot to write, not a loop
    // bound they got wrong.
    NdRankMismatch(want: Int, got: Int)
    // A reshape, or a construction from a list, whose element count
    // does not match the shape it was given.  `want` is the product of
    // the dims, `got` is the length of the buffer.
    NdSizeMismatch(want: Int, got: Int)
    // A reduction with no elements to reduce.  `sum` of nothing is 0.0
    // and needs no error.  `mean`, `min`, `max`, `argmin` and `argmax`
    // of nothing have no answer at all, and `what` names which one was
    // asked.
    NdEmptyReduction(what: Str)
    // A matrix operation on something that is not a matrix.  `dot`
    // wants two rank-1 arrays, and `matmul` wants rank 1 or 2 on each
    // side.  Anything else stops here rather than being guessed at.
    NdNotMatrix(what: Str, rank: Int)
    // A construction whose arguments describe no array.  That is a
    // negative dimension, a `linspace` of fewer than two points, or an
    // `arange` whose step is zero or points away from its stop.
    NdBadRange(what: Str)

// The rule every `NdFault` is printed by.  Say what was compared, and
// print both sides.
//
// `Result<T, E>` requires `E: Error` (SPEC § 3.4), so this
// implementation is what makes every fallible signature in the package
// spellable.
impl Error for NdFault
    fn message(self) -> Str
        match self
            NdShapeMismatch(want, got)      =>
                "shapes must match: ${want} and ${got}"
            NdNotBroadcastable(left, right) =>
                "shapes ${left} and ${right} do not broadcast"
            NdAxisOutOfRange(axis, rank)    =>
                "axis ${axis} on an array of rank ${rank}"
            NdIndexOutOfRange(index, dims)  =>
                "index ${index} is off an array of shape ${dims}"
            NdRankMismatch(want, got)       =>
                "an index of ${want} coordinate(s), not ${got}"
            NdSizeMismatch(want, got)       =>
                "a shape of ${want} element(s) over a buffer of ${got}"
            NdEmptyReduction(what)          =>
                "${what} of an empty array has no value"
            NdNotMatrix(what, rank)         =>
                "${what} needs a matrix, not an array of rank ${rank}"
            NdBadRange(what)                =>
                "${what} describes no array"
